// URL-loaded customization: projectionMenu
//
// Shows the projection button (MIP on/off and slab thickness) in the top-left
// action corner of every reconstructable viewport, after the orientation and
// data overlay menus. The button is registered by the cornerstone extension but
// is not part of the default corner menu, so a deployment or a mode opts in.
//
// It extends the default section layout registered by the cornerstone
// extension (`cornerstone.toolbarSections`) with an immutability-helper
// `$push`, so the built-in corner buttons are preserved. The `setProjectionMode`
// and `setSlabThickness` commands and the ProjectionService work without it.
//
// Load it with `?customization=tools/projectionMenu`, or list it in
// `customizationService` in the app config.
{
  "global": {
    "cornerstone.toolbarSections": {
      "viewportActionMenu.topLeft": {
        "$push": ["projectionMenu"]
      }
    }
  }
}
